# Data: ignore everything, keep only the sheets and the releasable benchmark
data/**
!data/
!data/DATASHEET.md
!data/SURVEYSHEET.md
!data/SYNTHSHEET.md
# Labelled data: nothing under data/labelled_data/ or data/labelled_data_v2/ is
# tracked except the prompt templates (prompts/ in each: every prompt a model
# sees, loaded by src/prompts.py and hashed by the review gate). The question
# bank's source of truth is src/synthesis/question_bank.py (tracked); the JSONL
# files mix licence tracks (NC text from SPoRC cannot be redistributed), and a
# releasable Track P copy is produced by `python -m src.synthesis.export --track p`.
!data/labelled_data/
data/labelled_data/*
!data/labelled_data/prompts/
!data/labelled_data/prompts/*.txt
!data/labelled_data/prompts/*.md
!data/labelled_data_v2/
data/labelled_data_v2/*
!data/labelled_data_v2/prompts/
!data/labelled_data_v2/prompts/*.txt
!data/labelled_data_v2/prompts/*.md

# Model weights and checkpoints
checkpoints/
outputs/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.ckpt

# wandb
wandb/
.wandb/

# Secrets. WANDB_API_KEY and any API keys come from the environment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local working notes
/notes.md
/CLAUDE.local.md

# Backstop only. Internal reference material must live outside the repo
# entirely, not here: an ignore rule is one `git add -f` or one careless
# edit away from failing, and an ignored file is invisible to the diff
# that confidentiality-check reads.
/context.md
*.private.md
/private/
transcript_description*
assessment*.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# vLLM evaluation environment
/.venv-vllm/
